  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Ellingham diagram is a graphical representation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi></math> vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> when metal heated with oxygen to form metal oxide.</p><p>An Ellingham diagram is a graph showing the temperature dependence of the stability for compounds. This analysis is usually used to evaluate the ease of reduction of metal oxides and sulphides.</p><p>Ellingham diagram represents change in free energy&nbsp;&Delta;G&nbsp;with temperature</p>"
